# Frontend environment — copy to .env.local ONLY if you need the override below.
#
# You usually do NOT need this file. By default the frontend derives the API
# URL from the address you opened the page on: browse to http://<host>:9098 and
# it calls http://<host>:9097 — correct for localhost and for a remote GPU host
# alike. See web/lib/apiBase.ts.
#
# Set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL only when the API is on a *different* host or domain
# than the UI (e.g. behind a reverse proxy, or split across two machines).
#
# WARNING: NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are compiled into the browser bundle at build
# time. Pointing this at localhost sends every visitor's browser to their own
# machine, not the server — and editing it after `npm run build` has no effect
# until you rebuild.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com

# Override only if the backend listens on a non-default port.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_PORT=9097
